      "value": "in case you end up here just as i did, it is indeed exposed, but in UdonSharp in `VRCShader` class, not just `Shader`.\n\nso `VRCShader.PropertyToID(\"prop_name\");`",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-12T19:34:52.503Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hi everone, as shader properties can be set from udon using for example: sharedMaterial.setColor( \"_name\", value ), these functions are also overloaded to accept name in the form of an integer id instead of string identifier.\nTo get this integer identifier, you call Shader.PropertyToID(\"_name\"), but this method is currently not exposed to Udon. It would be great have this method for performance reasons. every instruction counts =) \ncheers",
